[#- The rules of Renovate for what the osv-scanner.toml of the project accepts, as
    blueprint.py advisories writes them: in a Home Assistant integration those of the
    test tools that the blueprint accepts in stacks/home-assistant/, whose lock file a
    project has in its root, and none in every other project. Once the blueprint
    accepts none there, the render stops: then every kind takes the empty file. -#]
[%- from "includes/replace.jinja" import replaced with context -%]
[% if stack == 'home-assistant' -%]
{= replaced(".github/renovate-accepted.json5", [["stacks/home-assistant/", ""]]) -=}
[%- else -%]
// The versions that an osv-scanner.toml of this repository accepts with every
// advisory, as rules of Renovate, which .github/renovate-blueprint.json5 extends:
// Renovate opens no branch to fix a vulnerability of such a version, which the lock
// file couldn't take, as for a version that another package pins exactly. The command
// advisories of blueprint.py writes this file from the [[PackageOverrides]] of each
// osv-scanner.toml, and scripts/check.sh fails when they disagree; change those, not
// this file. https://github.com/Dennis-Otto/repo-blueprint
{
  "packageRules": []
}
[% endif -%]
